## Text

Section text is [CommonMark](https://commonmark.org/help/) Markdown:
_italic_, **bold**, `code` and [links](https://go.dev/).

- bullet lists
- with several items
  continued on the next line

1. numbered lists
2. work too

// A line starting with // is a comment and is not shown.

: Lines starting with ": " are speaker notes for this slide.
: Notes are Markdown: **bold**, `code` and [links](https://go.dev/) work.

::: notes
A block of notes holds longer notes:

- several paragraphs, lists and code
- lines starting with `#`, `.` or `//` are Markdown here too

It ends at a line with three colons.
:::

## Tables

[GitHub-style tables](https://github.github.com/gfm/#tables-extension-) line up with `|`;
colons in the separator row align the columns:

| Command  | Shows                  | Runs |
|----------|------------------------|:----:|
| `.code`  | source from a file     |  no  |
| `.play`  | source from a file     | yes  |
| `.image` | a picture or a diagram |  no  |

## Code blocks and quotes

Indented or fenced blocks are shown as code, without running anything:

```
$ go run golang.org/x/tools/cmd/present@latest
```

> Clear is better than clever.

\.play and the other commands start with a period; a backslash before it shows the line as text.

## Subsections

### A subsection starts with ###

Text under the subsection.

### Another subsection

#### Deeper levels use ####, ##### and so on

## Font size

.fontsize 3

fontsize 3

.fontsize 2

fontsize 2

.fontsize 0.8

fontsize 0.8

.fontsize 60%

fontsize 60%

.fontsize 0.45

fontsize 0.45

.fontsize

and `.fontsize` alone goes back to the default.

: Sizes are relative to the default size, not to the previous .fontsize.
: Absolute sizes work too: .fontsize 20px or .fontsize 14pt.

## Links and HTML

.link https://go.dev/ The **Go** website

.html html/badge.html

.iframe html/frame.html 120 600

: .link shows a single link on a line of its own; its label is inline Markdown.
: .html includes a file as raw HTML; .iframe embeds a page.

